{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-302070-r4518788","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Frito Pie Chili","sourcePageId":302070,"sourceRevision":"4518788","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:37:32Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Frito%20Pie%20Chili&oldid=4518788","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:54:20.218Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for chili","Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock","Category:Recipes using beef round","Category:Recipes using cayenne","Category:Recipes using chile flake","Category:Recipes using chili powder","Category:Recipes using corn flour","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Texas recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"5bd72a15112993282acb50cf990f3ab6f12e1a762312d1143f95484bd84bed33","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Chili recipes\n| Servings = 8\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThis chili is intended for use in [[Cookbook:Frito pie|frito pie]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] (30 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (475 ml) [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|Cayenne pepper]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] (900 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Beef#Round|beef bottom round]], cut into &#189;-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] (13 [[Cookbook:Mm|mm]]) cubes\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] (5 ml) [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|chili powder]]\n* 2 tsp (10 ml) ground [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]]\n* [[Cookbook:Red pepper flakes|Crushed red chile peppers]]\n* 2 tsp (10 ml) dried [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n* 2 Tbsp (30 ml) chopped [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 3 cups (710 ml) crushed [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* &#189; cup (120 ml) [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n* 2 cups (475 ml) beef [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]]\n* 1&#189; Tbsp (22 ml) [[Cookbook:Corn Masa|masa]]\n*1&#189; Tbsp (22 ml) [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# In a large [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]], heat the vegetable oil.\n# When the oil is hot, add the onions and [[Cookbook:Sautéing|sauté]] for 3 to 5 minutes, or until the vegetables start to wilt.\n# Season with salt and cayenne.\n# Stir in the beef, chili powder, cumin, crushed red pepper, and oregano. Brown the meat for 5 to 6 minutes.\n# Stir in the garlic, tomatoes, tomato paste, and beef stock.\n# Bring the liquid up to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] and reduce to a [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]]. Simmer the liquid, uncovered for 1 hour, stirring occasionally, or until the beef is tender. Skim off the fat occasionally.\n# Mix the masa and flour together with a little liquid from the stock pot.\n# Slowly stir in the masa slurry and continue to cook for 30 minutes, stirring occasionally.\n# Adjust salt, cayenne and other spices as needed.\n# Keep warm until ready to use or serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using beef round]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for chili]]\n[[Category:Texas recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile flake]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chili powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using corn flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Frito Pie Chili","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"8","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 Tbsp (30 ml) vegetable oil","sourceText":"2 Tbsp (30 ml) vegetable oil","amountText":"2 Tbsp (30 ml) vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cups (475 ml) chopped onions","sourceText":"2 cups (475 ml) chopped onions","amountText":"2 cups (475 ml) chopped onions","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Cayenne pepper","sourceText":"Cayenne pepper","amountText":"Cayenne pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 pounds (900 g) beef bottom round, cut into &#189;-inch (13 mm) cubes","sourceText":"2 pounds (900 g) beef bottom round, cut into &#189;-inch (13 mm) cubes","amountText":"2 pounds (900 g) beef bottom round, cut into &#189;-inch (13 mm) cubes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tsp (5 ml) chili powder","sourceText":"1 tsp (5 ml) chili powder","amountText":"1 tsp (5 ml) chili powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 tsp (10 ml) ground cumin","sourceText":"2 tsp (10 ml) ground cumin","amountText":"2 tsp (10 ml) ground cumin","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"Crushed red chile peppers","sourceText":"Crushed red chile peppers","amountText":"Crushed red chile peppers","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9